(a) A rectangle is $5$ cm longer than it is wide. Its perimeter is $50$ cm. Find its width.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=1mm,y=1mm]
\draw[black] (0,0) rectangle (45,25);
\path (22.5,25) node[above,text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont] {$w+5$ cm};
\path (0,12.5) node[left,text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont] {$w$ cm};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
(b) A father is four times as old as his son. In six years he will be three times as old as his son will be then. How old is the son now?

Write an equation for each scenario. Define the pronumeral first.
(a) Nine more than three times a number is $45$.
(b) Four identical boxes each contain $h$ pencils. Altogether they contain $36$ pencils.
(c) A green block represents $r$ and each red block represents $1$. The collection shown has total $18$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=1mm,y=1mm]
\definecolor{modelGreen}{HTML}{4F9B63}
\definecolor{modelRed}{HTML}{EF6068}
\draw[modelGreen] (0,0) rectangle (12,12);
\path (6,6) node[text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont] {$r$};
\foreach \x in {19,38,57} {
\draw[modelRed] (\x,0) rectangle +(12,12);
\path (\x+6,6) node[text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont] {$1$};
}
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

Form and solve an equation for each problem.
(a) Isla and Max have a combined age of $72$ years. Isla is twice as old as Max. How old is each person?
(b) A rectangle is three times as long as it is wide. Its perimeter is $80$ cm. Find its width.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=1mm,y=1mm]
\draw[black] (0,0) rectangle (54,18);
\path (27,18) node[above,text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont] {$3w$ cm};
\path (0,9) node[left,text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont] {$w$ cm};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
